"donor_log2fc":0.065859,"donor_lfcse":0.0778284,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":1.12818e-05,"degas_log2fc":-0.336844,"degas_padj":1.8723e-23},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"PLCE1","gene_symbol_current":"PLCE1","gene_id":"ENSG00000138193","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.942201,"donor_log2fc":0.0480096,"donor_lfcse":0.101837,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00472342,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000138193","module":"salmon","kme":0.44587,"hub":true,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.506562,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000138193","module":"salmon","kme":0.61663,"hub":true,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.655614,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Mic","gene_id":"ENSG00000138193","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0381114,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.398013,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000138193","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0493178,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000138193","entrez_id":["51196"],"uniprot":["Q9P212"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a phospholipase enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of phosphatidylinositol-4,5-bisphosphate to generate two second messengers: inositol 1,4,5-triphosphate (IP3) and diacylglycerol (DAG). These second messengers subsequently regulate various processes affecting cell growth, differentiation, and gene expression. This enzyme is regulated by small monomeric GTPases of the Ras and Rho families and by heterotrimeric G proteins. In addition to its phospholipase C catalytic activity, this enzyme has an N-terminal domain with guanine nucleotide exchange (GEF) activity. Mutations in this gene cause early-onset nephrotic syndrome; characterized by proteinuria, edema, and diffuse mesangial sclerosis or focal and segmental glomerulosclerosis. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants encoding distinct isoforms.[provided by RefSeq, Sep 2009].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9P212","text":"The production of the second messenger molecules diacylglycerol (DAG) and inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate (IP3) is mediated by activated phosphatidylinositol-specific phospholipase C enzymes. PLCE1 is a bifunctional enzyme which also regulates small GTPases of the Ras superfamily through its Ras guanine-exchange factor (RasGEF) activity. As an effector of heterotrimeric and small G protein, it may play a role in cell survival, cell growth, actin organization and T-cell activation. In podocytes, is involved in the regulation of lamellipodia formation. Acts downstream of AVIL to allow ARP2/3 complex assembly (PubMed:29058690)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}